{"content_hash": "416fc593b7f3fd6d", "version_id": 373, "article_id": 38, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Monaco Bomb Suspect Speaks from Kyiv Prison", "title_zh": "摩纳哥爆炸案嫌疑人基辅监狱打破沉默", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgel9044vqeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1612360262613-0b3388db84e9?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8c3VzcGVjdCUyMGxpbmtlZHxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTUwMzA1fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Franck V. on Unsplash", "author": "Franck V.", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@possessedphotography?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/silhouette-of-man-standing-near-window-vygLdyav_Wo?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(250, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(288, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "94a235c5d07a"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 259, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "A former Ukrainian security officer has spoken for the first time about a bomb attack in Monaco. He says senior members of Ukraine's military intelligence ordered it.", "lead_zh": "一名乌克兰前安全官员首次就摩纳哥爆炸案发声。他说，乌克兰军事情报机构的高级成员下令实施了这次袭击。", "preview": "Vitalii Zhykovych is a former Ukrainian security officer. He is in prison in Kyiv, and he spoke to the BBC with his lawyer. He said he belie", "preview_zh": "维塔利·日科维奇是一名乌克兰前安全官员。他目前被关押在基辅的监狱里，并在律师的陪同下接受了BBC的采访。他说，他认为摩纳哥的炸弹袭击是由乌克兰军事情报机构HUR的高级成员下令实施的。袭击发生在6月，目标是针对一位千万富翁商人。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 363, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/38/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 106.225, "size_bytes": 641088, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 292, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@ba94379/content/data/versions/373.json", "paragraphs": ["Vitalii Zhykovych is a former Ukrainian security officer. He is in prison in Kyiv, and he spoke to the BBC with his lawyer. He said he believed the bomb attack in Monaco was ordered by senior members of HUR, Ukraine's military intelligence agency. The attack happened in June and targeted a multi-millionaire businessman.", "The businessman, Vadym Yermolayev, and his 13-year-old son were badly hurt in the explosion. His partner also suffered terrible injuries. Yermolayev later said it was a miracle that they survived. A woman named Anastasia Berezovska was caught on camera leaving the bomb. Zhykovych says she was his agent.", "A week after the bombing, Berezovska's body was found in woods west of Kyiv. She had been shot in the head. Zhykovych says he did not send her to kill, and he did not kill her. He was arrested and accused of her murder, together with an active HUR officer called Vladyslav Reut.", "Reut first admitted to the murder and showed investigators where the body was. However, he later changed his story in court and blamed Zhykovych. Zhykovych now says Reut proposed the Monaco operation and told him it was official. He also says Reut provided the explosives and sent Berezovska to do the bombing without him.", "The case has caused a lot of speculation. People wonder who wanted Yermolayev dead and why. Zhykovych says Reut told him the attack was to punish Yermolayev for paying taxes in Russian-occupied Crimea. But Yermolayev denies any business links to Russia. The investigation continues, and Berezovska's family still have many questions."], "paragraphs_zh": ["维塔利·日科维奇是一名乌克兰前安全官员。他目前被关押在基辅的监狱里，并在律师的陪同下接受了BBC的采访。他说，他认为摩纳哥的炸弹袭击是由乌克兰军事情报机构HUR的高级成员下令实施的。袭击发生在6月，目标是针对一位千万富翁商人。", "这位商人名叫瓦季姆·叶尔莫拉耶夫，他和13岁的儿子在爆炸中受了重伤。他的伴侣也伤势严重。叶尔莫拉耶夫后来说，他们能活下来简直是奇迹。监控录像拍到一名叫阿纳斯塔西娅·别列佐夫斯卡的女子放置了炸弹。日科维奇说，她是他的特工。", "爆炸发生一周后，别列佐夫斯卡的尸体在基辅西部的树林里被发现。她头部中枪。日科维奇说，他没有派她去杀人，也没有杀她。他因此被捕，并被指控谋杀她，同时被指控的还有一名叫弗拉迪斯拉夫·雷乌特的HUR现役军官。", "雷乌特最初承认了谋杀，并带调查人员找到了尸体。然而，他后来在法庭上改变了说法，把责任推给日科维奇。日科维奇现在说，是雷乌特提出了摩纳哥的行动，并告诉他这是官方任务。他还说，雷乌特提供了炸药，并在没有他参与的情况下派别列佐夫斯卡去引爆炸弹。", "这起案件引发了大量猜测。人们想知道是谁想要叶尔莫拉耶夫死，以及为什么。日科维奇说，雷乌特告诉他，袭击是为了惩罚叶尔莫拉耶夫在俄罗斯占领的克里米亚纳税。但叶尔莫拉耶夫否认与俄罗斯有任何商业联系。调查仍在继续，别列佐夫斯卡的家人仍有许多疑问。"], "body": "Vitalii Zhykovych is a former Ukrainian security officer. He is in prison in Kyiv, and he spoke to the BBC with his lawyer. He said he believed the bomb attack in Monaco was ordered by senior members of HUR, Ukraine's military intelligence agency. The attack happened in June and targeted a multi-millionaire businessman.\n\nThe businessman, Vadym Yermolayev, and his 13-year-old son were badly hurt in the explosion. His partner also suffered terrible injuries. Yermolayev later said it was a miracle that they survived. A woman named Anastasia Berezovska was caught on camera leaving the bomb. Zhykovych says she was his agent.\n\nA week after the bombing, Berezovska's body was found in woods west of Kyiv. She had been shot in the head. Zhykovych says he did not send her to kill, and he did not kill her. He was arrested and accused of her murder, together with an active HUR officer called Vladyslav Reut.\n\nReut first admitted to the murder and showed investigators where the body was. However, he later changed his story in court and blamed Zhykovych. Zhykovych now says Reut proposed the Monaco operation and told him it was official. He also says Reut provided the explosives and sent Berezovska to do the bombing without him.\n\nThe case has caused a lot of speculation. People wonder who wanted Yermolayev dead and why. Zhykovych says Reut told him the attack was to punish Yermolayev for paying taxes in Russian-occupied Crimea. But Yermolayev denies any business links to Russia. The investigation continues, and Berezovska's family still have many questions.", "body_zh": "维塔利·日科维奇是一名乌克兰前安全官员。他目前被关押在基辅的监狱里，并在律师的陪同下接受了BBC的采访。他说，他认为摩纳哥的炸弹袭击是由乌克兰军事情报机构HUR的高级成员下令实施的。袭击发生在6月，目标是针对一位千万富翁商人。\n\n这位商人名叫瓦季姆·叶尔莫拉耶夫，他和13岁的儿子在爆炸中受了重伤。他的伴侣也伤势严重。叶尔莫拉耶夫后来说，他们能活下来简直是奇迹。监控录像拍到一名叫阿纳斯塔西娅·别列佐夫斯卡的女子放置了炸弹。日科维奇说，她是他的特工。\n\n爆炸发生一周后，别列佐夫斯卡的尸体在基辅西部的树林里被发现。她头部中枪。日科维奇说，他没有派她去杀人，也没有杀她。他因此被捕，并被指控谋杀她，同时被指控的还有一名叫弗拉迪斯拉夫·雷乌特的HUR现役军官。\n\n雷乌特最初承认了谋杀，并带调查人员找到了尸体。然而，他后来在法庭上改变了说法，把责任推给日科维奇。日科维奇现在说，是雷乌特提出了摩纳哥的行动，并告诉他这是官方任务。他还说，雷乌特提供了炸药，并在没有他参与的情况下派别列佐夫斯卡去引爆炸弹。\n\n这起案件引发了大量猜测。人们想知道是谁想要叶尔莫拉耶夫死，以及为什么。日科维奇说，雷乌特告诉他，袭击是为了惩罚叶尔莫拉耶夫在俄罗斯占领的克里米亚纳税。但叶尔莫拉耶夫否认与俄罗斯有任何商业联系。调查仍在继续，别列佐夫斯卡的家人仍有许多疑问。", "text": "Vitalii Zhykovych is a former Ukrainian security officer. He is in prison in Kyiv, and he spoke to the BBC with his lawyer. He said he believed the bomb attack in Monaco was ordered by senior members of HUR, Ukraine's military intelligence agency. The attack happened in June and targeted a multi-millionaire businessman. The businessman, Vadym Yermolayev, and his 13-year-old son were badly hurt in the explosion. His partner also suffered terrible injuries. Yermolayev later said it was a miracle that they survived. A woman named Anastasia Berezovska was caught on camera leaving the bomb. Zhykovych says she was his agent. A week after the bombing, Berezovska's body was found in woods west of Kyiv. She had been shot in the head. Zhykovych says he did not send her to kill, and he did not kill her. He was arrested and accused of her murder, together with an active HUR officer called Vladyslav Reut. Reut first admitted to the murder and showed investigators where the body was. However, he later changed his story in court and blamed Zhykovych. Zhykovych now says Reut proposed the Monaco operation and told him it was official. He also says Reut provided the explosives and sent Berezovska to do the bombing without him. The case has caused a lot of speculation. People wonder who wanted Yermolayev dead and why. Zhykovych says Reut told him the attack was to punish Yermolayev for paying taxes in Russian-occupied Crimea. But Yermolayev denies any business links to Russia. The investigation continues, and Berezovska's family still have many questions.", "vocab": [{"word": "bomb attack", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "炸弹袭击", "note": "指用炸弹进行的攻击"}, {"word": "suspect", "pos": "noun", "zh": "嫌疑人", "note": "警方认为可能犯罪的人"}, {"word": "prison", "pos": "noun", "zh": "监狱", "note": "关押犯人的地方"}, {"word": "military intelligence", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "军事情报", "note": "军队中负责收集情报的部门"}, {"word": "millionaire", "pos": "noun", "zh": "百万富翁", "note": "拥有超过一百万财富的人"}, {"word": "injure", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使受伤", "note": "常用被动语态 be injured"}, {"word": "agent", "pos": "noun", "zh": "特工", "note": "为情报机构工作的人"}, {"word": "murder", "pos": "noun", "zh": "谋杀", "note": "故意杀人"}, {"word": "explosive", "pos": "noun", "zh": "炸药", "note": "能引起爆炸的物质"}, {"word": "speculation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "猜测", "note": "没有证据的推测"}], "title_original": "Suspect linked to Monaco bomb attack on millionaire breaks silence to BBC", "summary_original": "Vitalii Zhykovych gives his own account of the attempted assassination of Ukrainian-born businessman Vadym Yermolayev.", "body_original": "Suspect linked to Monaco bomb attack on millionaire breaks silence to BBC\nBy\nSarah Rainsford\n,\nSouthern and Eastern Europe correspondent\nand\nMariana Matveichuk\nPublished\n2 hours ago\nA former Ukrainian security services officer linked to a bomb attack in Monaco in June that targeted a multi-millionaire says he believed it was ordered by senior members of HUR, Ukraine's military intelligence agency.\nIn an exclusive interview with the BBC from prison in Kyiv, facilitated by his lawyer, Vitalii Zhykovych has given his own account of the attempted assassination for the first time.\nUkrainian-born businessman Vadym Yermolayev and his 13-year-old son were badly hurt in the blast and his partner suffered catastrophic injuries. Yermolayev later described their survival as \"nothing short of a miracle\".\nZhykovych describes himself as a \"freelancer\" for Ukraine's SBU security service and says Anastasia Berezovska, the woman caught on camera planting the bomb in Monaco, was his \"agent\".\nA week after the bombing, Berezovska's body was discovered in the woods west of Kyiv with gunshot wounds to the head.\nBut Zhykovych insists he did not send her to kill, and nor did he kill her.\nHe was arrested and accused of her murder together with an active-duty intelligence officer from HUR called Vladyslav Reut.\nReut initially confessed to investigators, and led them to the shallow grave. But days later in court, he changed his testimony to blame Zhykovych.\nUkrainian agent accused of murdering Monaco bomb suspect changes story\nPublished\n9 July\nFor a long time, Zhykovych himself stayed silent.\nNow, responding to questions from the BBC, he alleges that Reut - who he refers to as \"The Boss\" - had \"proposed the operation\" in Monaco against Vadym Yermolayev.\nHe understood it was an official mission.\n\"As Reut informed me, this operation […] had been authorised and approved by Reut's superiors, who served in the Main Intelligence Directorate of the Ministry of Defence [HUR],\" he says.\nDistancing himself from the explosion itself, he alleges that Reut asked to use Berezovska for the bombing and when Zhykovych refused – he says she was not fully trained – Reut agreed to send her for reconnaissance instead.\nReut then communicated directly with Bereszovska without including him, according to Zhykovych, who alleges that Reut also provided her with the explosives.\nThe BBC asked HUR to comment on the latest claims. The agency has previously said that it is \"committed to a full investigation\" and providing \"comprehensive support\" to law enforcement bodies.\nThe SBU has described Zhykovych in a statement only as a \"former law enforcement officer\".\nYermolayev was attacked in Monaco as he and his family were returning from an evening meal on the seafront. A surveillance video shows Berezovska walking slightly in front of the group, then leaving the device in a bag on their doorstep.\nIt detonates just as they get close, apparently shocking even Berezovska with its force.\nYermolayev later said he believed that serving HUR officers, \"individuals close to the agency's current and former leadership\", were linked to the attack.\nHe called for \"the truth, protection, and justice\".\nBerezovska was quickly identified as the suspected bomber and on 2 July her image, taken from CCTV footage, was circulated by Interpol.\nShe had already fled, first driving through Italy and Germany, then taking a bus from Frankfurt to Ukraine.\nBefore she could be caught and questioned though, she was driven to the woods by Reut and Zhykovych and killed. Each blames the other for her shooting.\nThe shocking case has prompted intense speculation, including over who may have wanted Yermolayev dead and why, and whether this could have been a state-ordered assassination attempt, a rogue operation or some kind of criminal score-settling.\nThe businessman himself, who renounced his Ukrainian passport some years ago and now has Cypriot citizenship, has dismissed multiple theories.\nThey include the idea the attack might be linked to a struggle between organised crime groups involved in highly lucrative scam call-centres in Ukraine.\nEarlier this year, a court in Estonia convicted Yermolayev's son, Artur, of defrauding its citizens out of millions of euros through such \"offisy\", as the scam networks are known in Ukraine.\nVadym Yermolayev told the Ukrainska Pravda newspaper that he \"never had anything to do with anything\" in the case.\nNow Zhykovych has put forward his own theory to us.\nHe alleges that Reut told him the bombing was in retaliation for \"funding the annexation of Crimea\", which he understood to mean Yermolayev was paying taxes to Russia from businesses in Russian-occupied Crimea.\n\"In my view, this constitutes grounds for the operation,\" he communicated from prison.\nYermolayev has repeatedly denied any remaining business interests linked to Russia.\nBut might this story be even murkier?\nAt his most recent custody hearing in Kyiv, surrounded by heavily armed guards, Zhykovych spoke publicly for the first time since his arrest. The BBC were the only media present.\nAt one point Zhykovych said Reut had in fact told him the attack in Monaco was not \"authorised\".\n\"Someone had ordered this target from the civilian side,\" Zhykovych said, without explaining.\nThe judge then interrupted, reminding him that he was addressing an open court.\nZhykovych also revealed that Reut originally talked of two targets.\nWhen we asked, he said he could not disclose the second name. Other sources strongly suggest it was a pro-Russian blogger tried and convicted in absentia last year by Ukraine of treason.\nAs the investigation continues – into both the bombing in Monaco and the murder in Ukraine - Berezovska's family have many questions of their own.\nThe 39-year-old had been in Germany since early 2022, when she left Ukraine as a refugee with her young son.\nZhykovych now claims she was living a double-life, working with him as an agent \"against Muscovy\" – meaning Russia.\nHe said they had met online and told us the pair were working to \"repel the armed aggression of the Russian Federation\".\nBerezovska's husband has told the BBC that the allegation was \"nonsense\". He believes she was dragged, unwittingly, into the whole affair.\nZhykovych says Berezovska called him the day after the Monaco attack, and when he asked why she had done it, she said Reut had promised her a huge fee. \"$50,000 doesn't just lie on the streets,\" she supposedly explained.\nResidents in her village have told us that Berezovska was saving to buy a flat. But when she travelled to Ukraine to collect the money, she was lured into the woods and shot.\nAdditional reporting by Anastasiia Levchenko and Volodymyr Lozhko.\nRelated topics\nEurope\nKyiv\nUkraine\nMonaco\nMore on this story\nWoman suspected of Monaco bomb attack found dead in Ukraine\nPublished\n7 July", "fetched_a